UID:ef9ee64b2f3b015f@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T220717Z
SEQUENCE:2026091422
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 6:00 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 5:45 PM.\nOn stage: 7:00 PM–7:45 PM.\nACT I 
 Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — pr
 oduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time danc
 ers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Tim
 e.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiv
 ing and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are cal
 led unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedul
 e\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mast
 er: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N
 7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Fritz ***\nFritz —
  Costume (you provide): Black Tights\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeu
 p: Men's Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Neat and out of the eyes\; Prop (BA 
 provides): Hobby Horse\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Powde
 r matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease wi
 th an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara.
  No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so da
 ncer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Red or Dark Red
  lipstick\nMen's Stage Makeup:\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner - apply fr
 om corner to corner\n• Brown or tan under cheek bone to create shadow 
 and accentuate the jaw line\n• Brown eye liner around lips and nude/fl
 esh colored lipstick\n• *Men will not look like they are wearing makeu
 p. It will help the face be seen from the stage.\nDancers of Color may w
 ear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guideli
 nes:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent dama
 ge to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event
  of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant
 \n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costume
 s by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor while i
 n costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any c
 ostume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costume and 
 shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during
  its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while
  in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n•
  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the e
 xception of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressi
 ng rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secure h
 ead pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return all headpieces to th
 eir assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet A
 rkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored
  drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
