  Scene\, Battle Scene\, Snow Scene) (Mandatory – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 9:30 AM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 9:15 AM.\nOn stage: 10:30 AM–11:00 AM.\nACT 
 I Student Matinee Performance (to recorded sound)\; NO COFFEE\, BON BON\
 , ANGELS.\nMANDATORY — production week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA:
  Call Time is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive
  15 minutes before Call Time.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\,
  Rehearsals after Thanksgiving and Production Week Rehearsals and Perfor
 mances).\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANG
 E — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal ar
 e the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1x
 WFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKE
 UP — Fritz ***\nFritz — Costume (you provide): Black Tights\; Shoes:
  Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Men's Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Neat and 
 out of the eyes\; Prop (BA provides): Hobby Horse\nLight Stage Makeup In
 struction Sheet:\n• Powder matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shad
 ow applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black 
 eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be
  sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage l
 ights)\n• Red or Dark Red lipstick\nMen's Stage Makeup:\n• Dark Brow
 n/Black eyeliner - apply from corner to corner\n• Brown or tan under c
 heek bone to create shadow and accentuate the jaw line\n• Brown eye li
 ner around lips and nude/flesh colored lipstick\n• *Men will not look 
 like they are wearing makeup. It will help the face be seen from the sta
 ge.\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet s
 hoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care whi
 le changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify B
 allet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\
 , no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessories on 
 the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from s
 itting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend
 \, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply stage ma
 ke-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudgin
 g make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spr
 ay perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garment not a
 ssigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or beverage wh
 ile in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove costumes
  from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all 
 bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• 
 Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any 
 and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack
  markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain 
 costumes.
